What is Docker?

	Containerization platform – packages apps and dependencies into isolated containers

	Lightweight vs VMs (shares host OS kernel)

	Ensures "works on my machine" consistency

---------------------------------------------------

Key Concepts:

Concept				Description

Image				Blueprint/template (read-only) with app + dependencies

Container			Running instance of an image

Dockerfile			Script to build an image

Registry			Repository for images (e.g., Docker Hub)

Volume				Persistent data storage outside container

Network				Communication between containers


-----------------------------------------------------------

 Essential Commands

Images


docker build -t myapp:1.0 .          # Build image from Dockerfile
docker images                         # List images
docker rmi <image_id>                 # Remove image
docker pull nginx:latest              # Pull from registry
docker push myrepo/myapp:1.0          # Push to registry


-----------------------------------------------------------------


Containers


docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name web nginx   # Run container (detached)
docker ps                                    # List running containers
docker ps -a                                 # List all containers
docker stop <container>                      # Stop container
docker start <container>                     # Start stopped container
docker restart <container>                   # Restart
docker rm <container>                        # Remove container
docker exec -it <container> bash             # Enter running container
docker logs <container>                      # View logs
docker inspect <container>                   # Detailed info


----------------------------------------------------------------


Volumes


docker volume create mydata                  # Create volume
docker run -v mydata:/app/data ...           # Mount volume
docker run -v $(pwd):/app ...                # Bind mount (host path)


------------------------------------------------------------

Networks


docker network create mynet                  # Create network
docker run --network mynet ...               # Attach container
docker network ls                            # List networks

-----------------------------------------------------


Dockerfile Basics

dockerfile

	FROM node:18-alpine           # Base image
	WORKDIR /app                  # Working directory
	COPY package*.json ./         # Copy files
	RUN npm install               # Install deps
	COPY . .                      # Copy source
	EXPOSE 3000                   # Document port
	CMD ["npm", "start"]          # Run command


Best practices:

	Use alpine variants for smaller images

	Combine RUN commands to reduce layers

	Order layers from least to most frequently changing

------------------------------------------------------------

Docker Compose (Multi-container)

docker-compose.yml:


	version: '3.8'
	services:
	  web:
	    build: .
	    ports:
	      - "8080:80"
	    environment:
	      - NODE_ENV=production
	    depends_on:
	      - db
	    volumes:
	      - ./data:/app/data
	  
	  db:
	    image: postgres:15
	    environment:
	      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: secret
	    volumes:
	      - pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data

	volumes:
	  pgdata:


